Invariant : Something that does not change : अपरिवर्तनीय

A condition, Property, or Logical assertion that is guaranteed to remain unchanged throughout a specific phase of program execution.

Type 
      Loop Invariants
      Class / Object Invariants
      Data Type Invariants

Example

      Binary Search 
              Answer ALWAYS lies inside [l, r]
      
      Sliding Window
              Q : Longest substring without repeating chars
              I : Window always contains unique characters
      
      Two Pointer
              Q : Container with most water
              I : Area limited by shorter wall
      
      Heap
              Heap top always contains smallest/largest needed element
      
      BFS
              Queue contains nodes of current frontier

      DP
              Q : House Robber
              I : maximum money till index i



        

